(197089, 11120, 1005, '<td valign="top">Would this be the bassett hound sniffing a road sign?  (I just don''t see any trace of a road sign in this picture, brave to submit, but I feel sorry for the score you are getting.)  The dog''s nose is just too close, it makes for a fun/silly shot, but photo technically, it''s not good.  Very sad eyes.  Best I can go is a 3.  Swash</td>', 'Would this be the bassett hound sniffing a road sign?  (I just don''t see any trace of a road sign in this picture, brave to submit, but I feel sorry for the score you are getting.)  The dog''s nose is just too close, it makes for a fun/silly shot, but photo technically, it''s not good.  Very sad eyes.  Best I can go is a 3.  Swash', '2003-01-21 15:52:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(197090, 11335, 1005, '<td valign="top">Neat sun halos on the people walking towards you.  Well done shot for  the circumstances (shooting into the sun).  I see your road sign, but I cannot see the connection to your title.  I''m guessing, but is the title referring to the sidewalk glare?  Is this a place name?  Something in the man''s cup?  I''m also a bit conflicted about the challenge vs. your subjects (which seems to be the people).  O.K. the sign is the "action" (or in this case the NOT action {don''t walk}) and including the people is the who (shouldn''t be walking), I guess this works.  6 Swash</td>', 'Neat sun halos on the people walking towards you.  Well done shot for  the circumstances (shooting into the sun).  I see your road sign, but I cannot see the connection to your title.  I''m guessing, but is the title referring to the sidewalk glare?  Is this a place name?  Something in the man''s cup?  I''m also a bit conflicted about the challenge vs. your subjects (which seems to be the people).  O.K. the sign is the "action" (or in this case the NOT action {don''t walk}) and including the people is the who (shouldn''t be walking), I guess this works.  6 Swash', '2003-01-21 15:59:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(197092, 11342, 1005, '<td valign="top">Interesting perspective, but I''m afraid I don''t care for it that much.  I am missing the point of the narrow DOF, is the V more important than the vowels?  The close of a view lacks any points of reference, are these typed letters (small) or 12" tall letters?  The marks on the sign and lettering lead me to believe this "sign" has had a rough life.  The lettering itself is on the rough side (slightly home-made feel).   I get absolutely no emotional context, nothing to hold me to this shot.  5 Swash</td>', 'Interesting perspective, but I''m afraid I don''t care for it that much.  I am missing the point of the narrow DOF, is the V more important than the vowels?  The close of a view lacks any points of reference, are these typed letters (small) or 12" tall letters?  The marks on the sign and lettering lead me to believe this "sign" has had a rough life.  The lettering itself is on the rough side (slightly home-made feel).   I get absolutely no emotional context, nothing to hold me to this shot.  5 Swash', '2003-01-21 16:05:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(197093, 11149, 1005, '<td valign="top">Neat picture, I really like the big tree in the center of the frame.  I''m not seeing any kind of sign whatsoever, sorry (is it hiding?).  The "village" doesn''t look like any culture I''m familiar with (wood plank tee-pees?).  Shooting from shadows into sunlight is very tough, but this is pretty good (compliment!).  Sorry 5 Swash</td>', 'Neat picture, I really like the big tree in the center of the frame.  I''m not seeing any kind of sign whatsoever, sorry (is it hiding?).  The "village" doesn''t look like any culture I''m familiar with (wood plank tee-pees?).  Shooting from shadows into sunlight is very tough, but this is pretty good (compliment!).  Sorry 5 Swash', '2003-01-21 16:07:53.000000', NULL, 1),
