(197096, 11234, 1005, '<td valign="top">Neat colors.  A tripod really helps the shake.  (Did you want the shake?)  It''s nearly impossible to hold the camera THAT still for more than a second or so.  On my monitor the red "no" sign goes from pale red to strong red (left to right), could be parly due to the camera shake.  How in the world did you get the "no" sign to be looking this solid, while the rest of the frame is shaking like an earthquake?<br/>5 Swash</td>', 'Neat colors.  A tripod really helps the shake.  (Did you want the shake?)  It''s nearly impossible to hold the camera THAT still for more than a second or so.  On my monitor the red "no" sign goes from pale red to strong red (left to right), could be parly due to the camera shake.  How in the world did you get the "no" sign to be looking this solid, while the rest of the frame is shaking like an earthquake?5 Swash', '2003-01-21 16:11:18.000000', NULL, 1),
